WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.620
Sponges are strange creatures.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.120
Aside from being some of the

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.120
oldest extant species on Earth,

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.180
these invertebrates have a have an odd way

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.860
of maintaining rigidity in their bodies--glass.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.040
Sponges have hard structures within their bodies

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.560
called spicules, crystalline forms made from amorphous silica

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.540
that grow and branch to form wicked shapes.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.760
Researchers looked into how the sponge

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.200
forms these highly symmetrical structures,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.240
and how they become so complex.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.360
Under the microscope,

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.100
spicules from three different kinds of sponges

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.500
all have the same crystalline hexagonal structure,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.020
like a snowflake.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.700
Even though this basic structure

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.360
is the same across species,

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.820
the spicules then take many different shapes,

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.280
such as pointy needles,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.640
branched trees, or spiked spheres.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.840
Looking inside using X-ray nano-tomography

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.500
gives us a clue into how spicules develop.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.120
The internal scans show

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.760
that the proteins inside of spicules --

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.940
known as axial filaments --

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.340
predetermine the shape of the growing spicule.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.900
While all modern ways for humans to make glass

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.060
involve large amounts of heat, it turns out

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.720
that sponges don’t need this.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.060
Because the spicules

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.680
grow the crystalline branches

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.960
along a single filament whose structure

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.159
is determined by protein folding

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.440
whioh is a biological process based on how

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.560
amino acids in the protein chain

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.400
interact with each other.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.520
The sponges don’t need high temperatures

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.120
to generate these fine structures.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.240
This biological process is similar

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.300
to experimental technologies just making their way

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.360
into manufacturing for solar cells

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.240
and other electronics.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.720
So with a little more research, these ancient sponges

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.620
could make very modern technologies

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.620
easier to produce.

